/*
 * Copy-on-write support.
 *
 * When an export is exported with the copy-on-write option, writes are not
 * done to the master file, but to a per-connection diff file, which is
 * removed again when the connection is closed; as a result, the master file
 * is never modified, and all writes are lost upon disconnecting. Reads
 * check the diff file first, and fall back to the master file only for
 * pages that have not been written to.
 *
 * Two layouts for the diff file are supported. If the sparse_cow option is
 * in effect, the diff file is a sparse file as large as the export, and
 * every modified page is stored at the offset it has in the export. If it
 * is not, every modified page is appended to the end of the diff file in
 * the order in which pages are first modified; the position of a page in
 * the diff file is the number of pages before it which are present in the
 * diff file as well.
 *
 * In both layouts, a bitmap tracks which pages of the export are present
 * in the diff file. Pages are stored in the diff file in their entirety;
 * when a write covers only part of a page which is not in the diff file
 * yet, the remainder of the page is read from the master file so that the
 * page stored in the diff file is complete.
 */

